channelsstart
++ this is an example comment
++ for example, 0 = 0 means "Channel 0 uses instrument 0"

0 = 4
++ i changed the square to a sawtooth so im just gonna put square info here: dutycycle: "25" the valid numbers are 12.5, 25, 50,75, and all the numbers left of me but negative
++ if you arent using a channel just put an out of bounds number as the selected instrument or just dont write it at all

1 = 1
bent: "false"
++ the reason it says "bent" is cuz in some tracks like Once Upon A Time the triangle wave is bent backward

9 = 9
noise: "true"
PCMdrums: "false"

channelsend

notesstart
++ one number value (e.g. "10,") is one midi unit, if theres no spaces between a note and another note that means its held
++ if it has spaces between it that means its repeated
++ "0," is empty space
30: 65,65,65,65,65,65,65,65,68,68,68,68,68,68,68,68,70,70,70,70,68,68,68,68,65,65,65,65,65,65,65,65,
